    ],
    "summary": "Five drawers in one standalone base can't be built in Hex Cluster. A full base takes no drawers. A half base takes exactly one drawer, on its cut face. A quarter base takes none. Notch drawers and bays need two or three bases touching each other, which the brief rules out. The closest build I could make is one north-half base with one classic drawer on its cut face. The checks pass with no rule errors, and the mesh collision check reads clear."
